  <!-- ========== 3. 24-48H DELTA ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="delta">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      What Moved (Last 24-48h)
      <span class="meta">Descriptive · banned-verb lint enforced · each paragraph cites a forecast or is marked context-only</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="delta-narrative">
      <p>July 25, 2026 was the first night in thirteen consecutive days without an announced CENTCOM airstrike on Iranian territory. Trump stated publicly that the US is "locked and loaded" and a senior administration official, quoted by Reuters, characterized the pause as designed to demonstrate leverage before any return to talks — no mutual cessation was announced by either side. The prior strike-sequence pattern in this conflict shows each operational pause at 1-3 days before resumption. → moved <span class="cite">F9</span></p>

      <p>Iran rejected an Iraqi-intermediated US ceasefire proposal between July 21 and July 25, according to Reuters and two State Department officials quoted in the Washington Post. Iranian Foreign Ministry spokesman Esmail Baqaei stated that the US proposal lacked seriousness on the question of sanction relief. Qatar and Oman each submitted separately-authored ceasefire framework proposals to both parties on July 21 (Axios); no public US response to either proposal had been issued as of July 26. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>

      <p>IMF PortWatch (latest published July 19, 2026) recorded a 7-day rolling average of 15 commercial vessel transits per day through the Strait of Hormuz — 17% of the pre-crisis baseline of approximately 88 per day. Lloyd's List (July 21) recorded 70% of transits AIS-dark, up from 55% the prior week. Inbound Gulf traffic fell to 8 vessels in the most recent 7-day window, a post-MOU low. → supports <span class="cite">F11</span> without move</p>

      <p>Three separate ceasefire frameworks are currently active in the mediation track: the Qatar-Oman joint framework (July 21), a Saudi-backed proposal transmitted via Oman (July 23), and an Iraqi track that Iran publicly rejected (July 25). No common text has emerged from the three frameworks. The August 16 MOU 60-day endpoint falls 21 days from today and functions as the shared focal-point deadline for all active mediation tracks. → supports <span class="cite">F13</span> without move</p>
    </div>
  </div>

